 Grade Safari chapter Safari -- the state fold, the live camera, and the whole
 frame -- against wasm/safari.zig and wasm/render.zig.

 THE FRAME CHECK IS THE STRONGEST ORACLE IN THIS PROJECT and it is the one that
 was owed. `render.frame` is pub and it IS the frame: the backdrop, the ground,
 and everything that stands up in one depth order. Every check before this graded
 a drawer or a collection in isolation; the DISPATCH -- which kind gets drawn by
 what, in what order, with which focal -- lived in the browser poc and was graded
 by nothing at all. Now the port's whole frame is compared to the game's, command
 for command, at two states.

 What that catches which nothing else could: a kind dispatched to the wrong
 drawer, the depth order inverted, the backdrop drawn after the ground, the truck
 drawn before the rails, a drawer handed the base focal where the game hands it
 the live one. Each of those is a wrong SEQUENCE of otherwise-correct commands.

 THE FOLD IS GRADED AS A DEFINITION, not against safari.zig's own `advance`, and
 the reason is that module's surface (PORTING_NOTES E2 again). `advance` is an
 export over private statics with no setter, so it cannot be seeded and can only
 be run from the start line -- and NOTES section 4 rules out comparing
 trajectories, because two step functions in f32 and f64 diverge for reasons that
 are not the port's. What `advance` IS is four pub calls in a fixed order, so the
 probe composes those four and this grades one step from a shared state.

 THE ORDER IS THE POINT OF IT. The truck steps against the NEW rider distance;
 stepping it against the old one is a one-line difference that no single-module
 check can see, because both modules are right. Case 8 is the other branch: a
 state ON the finish line, where the whole ride restarts rather than stepping.

 THE CAMERA'S INGREDIENTS ARE GRADED SEPARATELY FROM THE MIX. `cat.focus`,
 `gaze.gazeFocus` and `camera.camFocal` are each pub, so `sf-catfocus` and
 `sf-gazefocus` are real oracles and `sf-focal` is their composition. A failure
 names which one moved. Three of the eight states have a live cat attention, two
 a live gaze, and one has both -- which is the case that decides whether the mix
 is a max or something else.

 THE FRAME'S COORDINATE GATE IS THE LOOSEST IN THE PORT, at 8e-5 relative, and it
 is one vertex that sets it: a tree trunk projected to x = -270,939 px, a quarter
 of a million pixels off the side of a 960-pixel canvas. The stream reddens at
 4e-5 and passes above it.

 THE AMPLIFIER IS x/forward, not the focal. A billboard is not near-clipped -- the
 collector drops it by SIZE, so a tree the rider is level with can still be drawn
 at a forward of centimetres -- and the perspective divide turns a micron of
 disagreement in that depth into pixels: dx = (x / forward) * d(forward), which at
 this vertex is about five million pixels per metre. The 2.5e-6 m behind it is
 D6's chain floor, unchanged; what changed is what multiplies it.

 So the gate is measuring a polygon no one can see, and that is the honest reading
 of it rather than a reason to drop the vertex: both sides compute it, it is in
 the buffer, and the blitter is what throws it away. D3 called this out when the
 first screen seam was calibrated -- an absolute gate fails far off screen, a
 relative one holds -- and this is the extreme end of the same curve.

 We say:

Section: The Ride States

  RideCase = record {
    seg : Integer,
    along : Real,
    across : Real,
    yaw : Real,
    v : Real,
    tilt : Real,
    heading : Real,
    gaze-yaw : Real,
    focus : Real,
    tpos : Real,
    tv : Real,
    clock : Real
  }

  ride-cases : List RideCase
  ride-cases = [RideCase { seg = 0, along = 0.0, across = 0.0, yaw = 0.0, v = 0.3, tilt = 0.0, heading = 0.0, gaze-yaw = 0.0, focus = 0.0, tpos = 500.0, tv = 0.3, clock = 0.0 }, RideCase { seg = 1, along = 600.0, across = 0.0, yaw = 0.0, v = 1.4, tilt = 0.02, heading = 0.6, gaze-yaw = 0.0, focus = 0.0, tpos = 1100.0, tv = 1.5, clock = 400.0 }, RideCase { seg = 1, along = 660.0, across = 0.2, yaw = 0.01, v = 1.4, tilt = 0.0, heading = 0.6, gaze-yaw = 0.0, focus = 0.0, tpos = 1180.0, tv = 1.5, clock = 460.0 }, RideCase { seg = 4, along = 150.0, across = 0.0 - 1.2, yaw = 0.0 - 0.22, v = 1.1, tilt = 0.30, heading = 1.4, gaze-yaw = 0.04, focus = 0.0, tpos = 2100.0, tv = 1.2, clock = 1500.0 }, RideCase { seg = 2, along = 300.0, across = 0.5, yaw = 0.05, v = 0.9, tilt = 0.06, heading = 0.9, gaze-yaw = 0.18, focus = 0.45, tpos = 1500.0, tv = 1.0, clock = 900.0 }, RideCase { seg = 6, along = 600.0, across = 0.0, yaw = 0.0, v = 2.4, tilt = 0.0, heading = 2.2, gaze-yaw = 0.0, focus = 0.0, tpos = 2900.0, tv = 2.0, clock = 2600.0 }, RideCase { seg = 12, along = 280.0, across = 0.6, yaw = 0.0 - 0.30, v = 1.3, tilt = 0.0 - 0.24, heading = 3.1, gaze-yaw = 0.0 - 0.12, focus = 0.8, tpos = 5000.0, tv = 1.1, clock = 4200.0 }, RideCase { seg = 18, along = 299.0, across = 0.0, yaw = 0.0, v = 1.0, tilt = 0.0, heading = 4.0, gaze-yaw = 0.0, focus = 0.0, tpos = 7400.0, tv = 1.0, clock = 6300.0 }]

  rider-of : RideCase -> RiderState
  rider-of (c) =
    RiderState { segment = c.seg, along = c.along, across = c.across, yaw = c.yaw, v = c.v, tilt = c.tilt, heading = c.heading, gaze-yaw = c.gaze-yaw, focus = c.focus }

 The fold's cases start the truck not braking; the frame's cases start it BRAKING,
 so the two brake panels and their halos are in the graded command stream.

  ride-of : RideCase, Boolean -> Ride
  ride-of (c) (braking) =
    Ride { rider = rider-of c, truck = TruckState { pos = c.tpos, v = c.tv, braking = braking }, clock = c.clock }

Section: The Live Camera

  cam-stream : List Segment, Integer -> List Real
  cam-stream (w) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ride-cases then []
    else [cat-attention w (rider-of (list-at ride-cases i))] & cam-stream w (i + 1)

  gaze-stream : Integer -> List Real
  gaze-stream (i) =
    if i >= list-length ride-cases then []
    else [gaze-focus (list-at ride-cases i).focus] & gaze-stream (i + 1)

  focal-stream : List Segment, Integer -> List Real
  focal-stream (w) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ride-cases then []
    else [ride-focal w (rider-of (list-at ride-cases i))] & focal-stream w (i + 1)

  vyaw-stream : Integer -> List Real
  vyaw-stream (i) =
    if i >= list-length ride-cases then []
    else [view-yaw-for (rider-of (list-at ride-cases i))] & vyaw-stream (i + 1)

  roll-stream : Integer -> List Real
  roll-stream (i) =
    if i >= list-length ride-cases then []
    else [rider-roll (rider-of (list-at ride-cases i))] & roll-stream (i + 1)

Section: The Fold

  folded : List Segment, Integer -> List Ride
  folded (w) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ride-cases then []
    else [ride-next w (ride-of (list-at ride-cases i) False)] & folded w (i + 1)

  f-along : List Ride, Integer -> List Real
  f-along (rs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length rs then []
    else [(list-at rs i).rider.along] & f-along rs (i + 1)

  f-v : List Ride, Integer -> List Real
  f-v (rs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length rs then []
    else [(list-at rs i).rider.v] & f-v rs (i + 1)

  f-seg : List Ride, Integer -> List Integer
  f-seg (rs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length rs then []
    else [(list-at rs i).rider.segment] & f-seg rs (i + 1)

  f-tpos : List Ride, Integer -> List Real
  f-tpos (rs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length rs then []
    else [(list-at rs i).truck.pos] & f-tpos rs (i + 1)

  f-tv : List Ride, Integer -> List Real
  f-tv (rs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length rs then []
    else [(list-at rs i).truck.v] & f-tv rs (i + 1)

  f-brake : List Ride, Integer -> List Boolean
  f-brake (rs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length rs then []
    else [(list-at rs i).truck.braking] & f-brake rs (i + 1)

  f-clock : List Ride, Integer -> List Real
  f-clock (rs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length rs then []
    else [(list-at rs i).clock] & f-clock rs (i + 1)

Section: The Frame

 Two states: the hard lean, where the live focal is doing something to every
 projection, and the long straight at speed with the truck close.

  frame-cases : List Integer
  frame-cases = [3, 5]

  frame-wire : List Segment, Integer -> List DrawCmd
  frame-wire (w) (i) =
    if i >= list-length frame-cases then []
    else (ride-frame w (ride-of (list-at ride-cases (list-at frame-cases i)) True)) & frame-wire w (i + 1)

  s-tags : List DrawCmd, Integer -> List Integer
  s-tags (cs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length cs then []
    else [(list-at cs i).tag] & s-tags cs (i + 1)

  s-cols : List DrawCmd, Integer -> List Integer
  s-cols (cs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length cs then []
    else [(list-at cs i).color] & s-cols cs (i + 1)

 A BEACON HAS NO POINTS and reports zero, which is what the probe records for it:
 its centre and radius ride in `geom`, and `pts` is empty by the rule Paint's own
 prose sets out. Every other tag reports its polygon's length.

  s-counts : List DrawCmd, Integer -> List Integer
  s-counts (cs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length cs then []
    else [list-length (list-at cs i).pts / 2] & s-counts cs (i + 1)

 EVERY TWENTY-FOURTH POINT, and the thinning is C7's ceiling rather than a choice:
 two frames are about 44,000 coordinates and one Codex Real literal past roughly
 16,868 exhausts the transpiler's own bump heap. Counts stay exact, so a command
 that gained or lost a point fails hard regardless; what thins is the density.

  keep-nth : Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  keep-nth (k) (n) = k - (k / n) * n == 0

  every-nth : List Real, Integer, Integer -> List Real
  every-nth (ps) (i) (n) =
    if i + 1 >= list-length ps then []
    else if keep-nth (i / 2) n then [list-at ps i, list-at ps (i + 1)] & every-nth ps (i + 2) n
    else every-nth ps (i + 2) n

  thin-coords : List DrawCmd, Integer -> List Real
  thin-coords (cs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length cs then []
    else (every-nth (list-at cs i).pts 0 24) & thin-coords cs (i + 1)

Section: Entry

  segs : List Segment
  segs = build-world

  all-folded : List Ride
  all-folded = folded build-world 0

  all-frame : List DrawCmd
  all-frame = frame-wire build-world 0

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (grade-rel   "sf-catfocus  " (cam-stream segs 0) g-sf-catfocus 0.000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-rel   "sf-gazefocus " (gaze-stream 0) g-sf-gazefocus 0.000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-rel   "sf-focal     " (focal-stream segs 0) g-sf-focal 0.000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-rel   "sf-viewyaw   " (vyaw-stream 0) g-sf-viewyaw 0.000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-rel   "sf-roll      " (roll-stream 0) g-sf-roll 0.000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-rel   "sf-fold-along" (f-along all-folded 0) g-sf-fold-along 0.000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-rel   "sf-fold-v    " (f-v all-folded 0) g-sf-fold-v 0.000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "sf-fold-seg  " (f-seg all-folded 0) g-sf-fold-seg)
    print-line-uni (grade-rel   "sf-fold-tpos " (f-tpos all-folded 0) g-sf-fold-tpos 0.000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-rel   "sf-fold-tv   " (f-tv all-folded 0) g-sf-fold-tv 0.000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "sf-fold-brake" (f-brake all-folded 0) g-sf-fold-brake)
    print-line-uni (grade-rel   "sf-fold-clock" (f-clock all-folded 0) g-sf-fold-clock 0.000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "sf-frame-tag " (s-tags all-frame 0) g-sf-frame-tag)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "sf-frame-col " (s-cols all-frame 0) g-sf-frame-col)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "sf-frame-cnt " (s-counts all-frame 0) g-sf-frame-cnt)
    print-line-uni (grade-px    "sf-frame-xy  " (thin-coords all-frame 0) g-sf-frame-xy 0.001 0.00008)
  end
